 with structure in ways  that we could not have observed if we  had not made the measurement the way  that we did that is to say with high  resolution using the micro electrode  array and this is really important for  clinical applications because the  different types of events need to be  diagnosed differently and the treatment  that the patients will receive should  reflect this diagnosis then in  conclusion I've told you about how Phil  potentials can be used to interpret and  understand the organization of brain  activity and the functional forward  model is a very important concept for  this because it allows us to interpret  the selectivity in the signals and how  we use them to understand neural  computations I've also shown you how we  can develop a framework for analyzing  your computations that's been used to  study visually guided behaviors and  animals and to do so for what is a  uniquely human faculty that of speech  I've presented how we can translate new  technologies that are low cost and high  resolution that will allow us to resolve  dynamics in more detailed ways than we  could before and offer new treatment  paradigms we hope thank you very much  thank you dr. Peston for that excellent  talk as a reminder our speaker will  follow up any questions about his  presentation by email  continuing with our innovative  neurotechnologies track we have the  outstanding dr. Georges Ozaki presenting  next Doctor Who sakis top title is high  resolution recording and non-invasive  perturbation tools for the human brain  hope to see you there
 

